Static map
A static map is an image that cannot be changed by the user.

For example, a static map may be:
part of a published report on crime rates
generated by a service based on information provided by a user
Interactive map
An interactive map allows the users to change what the map is showing.

For example, an interactive map may allow users to :
Zoom to show larger or smaller area of the map
plot a route or area
draw areas or routes on to the map
change the time
view different layers of information


